<title>FRANCE: Cheuvreux, CCF turn buyers on Legris.</title>
<headline>Cheuvreux, CCF turn buyers on Legris.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>French broker Cheuvreux de Virieu changed its recommendation on Legris Industries to buy from sell citing better visibility on the company, fund managers said on Monday.</p>
<p>CCF Elysees Bourse also told Reuters it had changed its rating on the stock to buy from increase.</p>
<p>Both brokerages made the changes after the company held an analysts' meeting last week. Legris closed up 1.41 percent to 273.8 francs in a volume of 55,947 shares.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5432</p>
</text>
